  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than a data or information error, so resubmission or providing records is not the correct next step. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid, non-escalating action to challenge the bundling determination. This is preferable to an appeal at this stage as it is a faster, less formal route to overturn a clinical denial.",
